  "id": "nhs-10-min-toning",
  "title": "10-minute home toning workout",
  "creator": "NHS",
  "description": "A full-body toning circuit from the NHS 10-minute series: press-ups, dips, band presses, curls and raises, squats, lunges, crunches and back raises, mostly two sets each. It needs a resistance band, or water bottles as a stand-in. Sets are 12 to 24 reps; drop to the three-quarter press-up and floor dips if the full versions are too hard. Warm up first with the NHS 6-minute warm-up (nhs-6-min-warm-up) and finish with the 5-minute stretch (nhs-5-min-cool-down-stretch).",
